    <!-- The users table itself has always been managed by Hibernate's ddl-auto
         (now `validate`); Liquibase is only introduced here for this one
         change, which Hibernate can't express: enforcing email uniqueness at
         the database level. Both changesets operate on the table, not create
         it, so they assume it already exists. -->
